// RUN: %t.moves | FileCheck %s

// Frame 0 is every query's first run: every bar is redrawn; the repairs
// add shields, which @restored (after them in the frame) counts.
// CHECK:      frame 0 ship 0: hp 100 width 100 redraws 1 alarms 0 restores 1 shield 1
// CHECK-NEXT: frame 0 ship 1: hp 100 width 100 redraws 1 alarms 0 restores 1 shield 1
// CHECK-NEXT: frame 0 ship 2: hp 100 width 100 redraws 1 alarms 0 restores 1 shield 1
// Frame 1: only ship 1 changed (hp 40) and lost its shield.
// CHECK-NEXT: frame 1 ship 0: hp 100 width 100 redraws 1 alarms 0 restores 1 shield 1
// CHECK-NEXT: frame 1 ship 1: hp 40 width 40 redraws 2 alarms 1 restores 1 shield 0
// CHECK-NEXT: frame 1 ship 2: hp 100 width 100 redraws 1 alarms 0 restores 1 shield 1
// Frame 2: ship 1 is repaired and regains its shield.
// CHECK-NEXT: frame 2 ship 0: hp 100 width 100 redraws 1 alarms 0 restores 1 shield 1
// CHECK-NEXT: frame 2 ship 1: hp 100 width 100 redraws 3 alarms 1 restores 2 shield 1
// CHECK-NEXT: frame 2 ship 2: hp 100 width 100 redraws 1 alarms 0 restores 1 shield 1
// Frame 3: nothing happened, nothing is collected.
// CHECK-NEXT: frame 3 ship 0: hp 100 width 100 redraws 1 alarms 0 restores 1 shield 1
// CHECK-NEXT: frame 3 ship 1: hp 100 width 100 redraws 3 alarms 1 restores 2 shield 1
// CHECK-NEXT: frame 3 ship 2: hp 100 width 100 redraws 1 alarms 0 restores 1 shield 1
